WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — ai-reads-human (60s) Narrator Sean

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.080
JSON, YAML, and Markdown evolved so humans could

2
00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.172
inspect files in text editors—not for billion-record agent loops.

3
00:00:09.692 --> 00:00:14.496
Before a transformer even runs one matrix multiply,

4
00:00:14.496 --> 00:00:21.939
cl100k_base JSON tokenization burns 12.5 times more energy than C JSON parsing.

5
00:00:22.459 --> 00:00:25.827
Across 20,000 structured records,

6
00:00:25.827 --> 00:00:34.705
per-process L3 reported_j spans 2,053.8x from fixed binary structs to pure-Python YAML.

7
00:00:35.225 --> 00:00:40.859
Human formats also smuggle silent parsing bugs—from YAML's Norway

8
00:00:40.859 --> 00:00:46.232
boolean trap to IEEE float truncation and duplicate JSON keys.

9
00:00:46.752 --> 00:00:57.511
Falsifier 6 automatically flags noisy whole-SoC L2 windows while preserving clean per-process L3 reported_j receipts.
